The property is **`tokenizerId`** on the simulator's submit outcome.

From the test in `packages/core/test/cache.test.ts` (the `'records the injected tokenizer id on every outcome…'` case under "Zone A — the frozen prefix (§10 rule 5, D5)"):

```ts
const heuristic = new ProviderCacheSimulator({ tokenizer: h.tokenizer }).submit(prompt);
const bytes = new ProviderCacheSimulator({
  tokenizer: new ExactTokenizer('bytes-v0', (text) => text.length),
}).submit(prompt);

expect(bytes.tokenizerId).toBe('bytes-v0');                    // ← the property
expect(bytes.total).not.toBe(heuristic.total);
expect(bytes.segments.map((s) => s.blockIds)).toEqual(heuristic.segments.map((s) => s.blockIds));
```

So `bytes` is the `ProviderCacheSimulator.submit(prompt)` outcome, and `bytes.tokenizerId` is the assertion expected to equal `'bytes-v0'` — the test verifies the injected tokenizer's id is recorded on every outcome (so a tokenizer swap shows up as a deliberate diff rather than silently shifting every recorded range), while the segment structure (`blockIds` sequence) stays identical between the byte-exact and heuristic tokenizers.
